; CLIP.INF - written by SceneDesk for scene S010, the 320x200 edition. The recipe is
; tracked; the CLIP.OWV it makes is not, until the codec is frozen. The source is
; named relative to this folder: long, but it holds wherever the warehouse
; sits beside the repository.

SOURCE     = ..\..\..\..\..\..\..\OWLFLY4_RES\NIGHT\S010\VIDEO\grok-video-81d38084-ecf1-4d47-822c-c78be319573b.mp4
OUTPUT     = CLIP.OWV
WIDTH      = 320
HEIGHT     = 200
FPS        = 12
; 72 frames = six seconds, the unit the footage is generated in: every
; six-second piece is its own keyframe group, so a clip can later be cut
; at those boundaries without converting it again.
KEYEVERY   = 72
AUDIO      = 22050
; sixteen bits: the Sound Blaster 16 plays them and eight bits hiss
AUDIOBITS  = 16
FIT        = crop
DITHER     = bayer:bayer_scale=3
DENOISE    = hqdn3d=4:3:12:9
TOLERANCE  = 2
; GRAIN and SNAP buy bitrate with picture, and BOTH ARE OFF: the size
; problem they were written for is answered by streaming the clips
; instead, and what the player sees is worth more than the megabytes.
; They cost the encoder only - the format and the DOS player know
; nothing of either - so turning them up later needs no new player.
;
; GRAIN is how many of a block's 64 pixels may be past TOLERANCE and
; the block still be left alone: grain is a few pixels, motion is many,
; and counting them tells the two apart where an average does not.
; SNAP moves a pixel onto the one before it when it is already that
; close, so the ordered dither leaves runs for the RLE coder.
;
; Measured on S01's second clip: 12.4 MB here, 9.2 MB at GRAIN 8,
; 5.5 MB at GRAIN 12 with SNAP 2 - and the last one shows.
GRAIN      = 0
SNAP       = 0
SEARCH     = 24
COPY       = on
COPYSEARCH = 4
AUDIOFILTER = highpass=f=50,acompressor=threshold=0.06:ratio=4:attack=5:release=200:makeup=2,alimiter=limit=0.97
